{"abstract":"This paper analyses the visual digital images of nature shared by climate activists in Germany and Argentina, with a focus on affective nature representations. We show that activist communities in Argentina represent nature in diverse, affective ways while their counterparts in Germany visually present nature less often, while highlighting a scientifically mediated, fact-based representation of global climate change. Our comparative study shows how varying national political and cultural contexts and populist media debates shape the visual representation of human-nature relationships online. We discuss climate activists’ social media constructions of imaginaries for the future of ecological transitioning and North-South solidarity bridging narratives of science, affect, and non-human subjects characters in digital storytelling.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Doerr, Nicole","Langa, María Florencia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754969"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"images of nature in online climate activism in germany and argentina science affect and non human everybodies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/401197758/doerr_langa_post_print.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754969","identifier":[{"id":"85203335900","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e78f73f5-1bf9-44cc-a145-02bdb0b2adda"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E523B69E1D5E5C98EAB7571DB024B49F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/401197758/doerr_langa_post_print.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Sociology, Department of Sociology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nicole","key":"doerrpau","last":"Doerr","locid":"986666d1-830b-4ec9-a649-73db8d9f4f15","name":"Doerr, Nicole","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"María Florencia","key":"langapau","last":"Langa","locid":"4b6d8e0c-fbba-4bbe-96f0-6c1f8927a11f","name":"Langa, María Florencia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.20446/jep-2414-3197-40-1-33","issn":["24143197"],"issue":"3-4","journal":"Journal für Entwicklungspolitik","pages":"33-64","status":"p","title":"Journal für Entwicklungspolitik","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203335900"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e78f73f5-1bf9-44cc-a145-02bdb0b2adda"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Images of Nature in Online Climate Activism in Germany and Argentina : Science, Affect and Non-Human ‘Everybodies’","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754969","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
